<</Names[(NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:*  This summary does not include participants with a primary disability of Down syndrome. 1:36)[6 0 R/XYZ 22 43 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:*  This summary does not include participants with a primary disability of Down syndrome.:37)[6 0 R/XYZ 22 43 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:1. The Australian Bureau of Statistics SEIFA Index of Education and Occupation \(IEO\) is used by NDIA:21)[172 0 R/XYZ 22 520 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:10.  A registered provider is an approved person or provider of supports who is registered with the:30)[172 0 R/XYZ 22 182 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:2. Supported Independent Living \(SIL\) is help with and/or supervision of daily tasks to develop the:22)[172 0 R/XYZ 22 459 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:3. Average payments per participant are calculated using a 12 month period prior to the reporting da:23)[172 0 R/XYZ 22 435 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:4. The average payment for the same group of participants is compared across two different time peri:24)[172 0 R/XYZ 22 421 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:5. The Participant Outcome section compares baseline results when participants entered the Scheme or:25)[172 0 R/XYZ 22 381 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:6. The NDIA gathers responses at the four primary stages of the participant pathway - access, pre-pl:26)[172 0 R/XYZ 22 320 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:7. The complaint rate is an annualised rate calculated as the number of complaints in the quarter di:27)[172 0 R/XYZ 22 281 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:8. The count of providers is by ABN and includes providers supporting agency-managed participants, p:28)[172 0 R/XYZ 22 252 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:9. For each plan management type, a single provider is counted if they received a payment in the qua:29)[172 0 R/XYZ 22 217 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:Insights:15)[6 0 R/XYZ 22 1245 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:Insights:33)[6 0 R/XYZ 22 1245 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:Insights:9)[6 0 R/XYZ 22 1245 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:Key definitions:20)[172 0 R/XYZ 22 587 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:Key definitions:32)[172 0 R/XYZ 22 587 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:Section 1: Participants:10)[14 0 R/XYZ 23 1064 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:Section 1: Participants:16)[14 0 R/XYZ 23 1064 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:Section 2: Payments:11)[119 0 R/XYZ 22 898 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:Section 2: Payments:17)[119 0 R/XYZ 22 898 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:Section 3: Participant outcomes and satisfaction:18)[135 0 R/XYZ 22 637 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:Section 4: Providers:13)[153 0 R/XYZ 22 878 null](NDIS218_Dashboard_DD_Sep23_P4.indd:Section 4: Providers:19)[153 0 R/XYZ 22 878 null]]>>
